/*
We have two lanes, each of length 1 (only relative times matter).
Swimmer i has pace p_i = time to swim one length.
Each swimmer plans to swim l_i lengths.

Rules:
- All start simultaneously from the same end.
- In a lane, swimmers cannot overtake except at the ends.
- Thus during a single length, a group in one lane moves at the slowest swimmer's pace in front.
- At each end, swimmers may reorder by natural pace.

Key observation:
Because reordering is allowed at every end, for each single length independently we can assign
the swimmers who still need to swim that length into two lanes so that the completion time of
that "round" equals the maximum of the slowest swimmer in each lane.
If swimmers assigned to one lane for a round are a set S, that lane's round time is max(p_i in S).
Therefore for the active swimmers in a round, if we sort their paces descending:
q1 >= q2 >= q3 ...
the optimal split into two lanes is:
- lane 1 gets q1
- lane 2 gets q2, q3, ...
giving round time q2 (if at least 2 swimmers), or q1 if only 1 swimmer.
Equivalently, the round time is the second largest pace among swimmers still active,
or the largest if only one swimmer remains.

If swimmer i needs l_i lengths, then swimmer i is active in rounds 1..l_i.
So for each round t, among swimmers with l_i >= t, add:
- max pace if count=1
- second largest pace if count>=2

We process rounds by grouping swimmers by lap count descending.
Maintain multiset of active paces and query largest / second largest quickly.
A TreeMap pace->count suffices.

Input format assumed:
n
p1 l1
p2 l2
...
pn ln

Output:
total time

We use long throughout.
*/
public class Main {
    static class Swimmer {
        long pace;
        int laps;
        Swimmer(long pace, int laps) {
            this.pace = pace;
            this.laps = laps;
        }
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner(System.in);
        int n = fs.nextInt();
        if (n == Integer.MIN_VALUE) return;

        Swimmer[] arr = new Swimmer[n];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            long p = fs.nextLong();
            int l = fs.nextInt();
            arr[i] = new Swimmer(p, l);
        }

        Arrays.sort(arr, (a, b) -> Integer.compare(b.laps, a.laps));

        TreeMap<Long, Integer> active = new TreeMap<>();
        long activeCount = 0;
        long total = 0;

        int idx = 0;
        int currentLap = (n > 0 ? arr[0].laps : 0);

        while (currentLap > 0) {
            while (idx < n && arr[idx].laps == currentLap) {
                add(active, arr[idx].pace);
                activeCount++;
                idx++;
            }

            int nextLap = (idx < n ? arr[idx].laps : 0);
            int rounds = currentLap - nextLap;

            if (activeCount == 1) {
                total += rounds * active.lastKey();
            } else if (activeCount >= 2) {
                long largest = active.lastKey();
                Map.Entry<Long, Integer> e = active.lastEntry();
                long secondLargest;
                if (e.getValue() >= 2) {
                    secondLargest = largest;
                } else {
                    secondLargest = active.lowerKey(largest);
                }
                total += rounds * secondLargest;
            }

            currentLap = nextLap;
        }

        System.out.println(total);
    }

    static void add(TreeMap<Long, Integer> map, long x) {
        map.put(x, map.getOrDefault(x, 0) + 1);
    }

    static class FastScanner {
        private final InputStream in;
        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1 << 16];
        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;

        FastScanner(InputStream is) {
            in = is;
        }

        private int read() throws IOException {
            if (ptr >= len) {
                len = in.read(buffer);
                ptr = 0;
                if (len <= 0) return -1;
            }
            return buffer[ptr++];
        }

        int nextInt() throws IOException {
            long v = nextLong();
            if (v == Long.MIN_VALUE) return Integer.MIN_VALUE;
            return (int) v;
        }

        long nextLong() throws IOException {
            int c;
            do {
                c = read();
                if (c == -1) return Long.MIN_VALUE;
            } while (c <= ' ');

            int sign = 1;
            if (c == '-') {
                sign = -1;
                c = read();
            }

            long val = 0;
            while (c > ' ') {
                val = val * 10 + (c - '0');
                c = read();
            }
            return val * sign;
        }
    }
}

